/*
** The play-of-colour switch.
**
** This control used to disable two infinite `animation`s (the masthead shimmer
** and the selected-tab sheen). Both animations are gone, so the old rule would
** have left a ControlPanel checkbox that silently did nothing. It now governs
** the thing a reader would actually want a switch for: the iridescence itself.
**
** Turning it off flattens `--o-fire` to a solid accent, so every band that
** carried it — the masthead segment, the selected tab, the edit-mode panel
** edge — stays exactly where it is and keeps its contrast, but stops being
** iridescent. One override does all of them because they all draw from the
** same token.
**
** Focus rings are deliberately NOT affected: they use `--o-fire-a`, a single
** colour rather than the gradient, so the accessibility indicator is identical
** either way.
*/

{{{ [[$:/config/themes/opaline/fire]get[text]match[no]then[:root{--o-fire:linear-gradient(90deg,var(--o-accent-ink),var(--o-accent-ink));}]] }}}
